{"tool_name":"lutefisk","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"lutefisk","home":"http://www.hairyfatguy.com/lutefisk","summary":"\"De novo\" peptide sequencing from MS/MS data.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:51:11Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:14:32.145930Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:lutefisk","credit":[{"email":"JohnsonR@immunex.com","name":"Johnson R","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Maintainer"]},{"email":"webmaster@ms-utils.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"http://ms-utils.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.hairyfatguy.com/lutefisk/docs/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry spectra","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0943"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"},{"term":"dta","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3652"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence set","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0850"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Validation of peptide-spectrum matches","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3648"},{"term":"de Novo sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3644"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0850"},"format":[{"term":"Sequence record format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1919"}]}]}],"name":"lutefisk","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"msutils_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1385/mb:22:3:301","metadata":{"abstract":"There are many computer programs that can match tandem mass spectra of peptides to database-derived sequences; however, situations can arise where mass spectral data cannot be correlated with any database sequence. In such cases, sequences can be automatically deduced de novo, without recourse to sequence databases, and the resulting peptide sequences can be used to perform homologous nonexact searches of sequence databases. This article describes details on how to implement both a de novo sequencing program called \"Lutefisk,\" and a version of FASTA that has been modified to account for sequence ambiguities inherent in tandem mass spectrometry data.","authors":[{"name":"Johnson R.S."},{"name":"Taylor J.A."}],"citationCount":73,"date":"2002-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Applied Biochemistry and Biotechnology - Part B Molecular Biotechnology","title":"Searching sequence databases via de novo peptide sequencing by tandem mass spectrometry"},"pmid":"12448884"}],"topic":[{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"lutefisk","home":"https://bio.tools/lutefisk","summary":"\"De novo\" peptide sequencing from MS/MS data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:lutefisk/app/www.hairyfatguy.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":18,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":1,"year":"2019"},{"count":2,"year":"2007"},{"count":2,"year":"2015"},{"count":3,"year":"2005"},{"count":3,"year":"2010"},{"count":3,"year":"2011"},{"count":3,"year":"2013"}],"doi":"10.1385/MB:22:3:301","pmid":"12448884","ref_count":21,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1986"},{"count":1,"year":"1988"},{"count":1,"year":"1995"},{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":2,"ye